## Structural Map

Key files Claude reads first:
- `src/main.rs` — entry point, router and state wiring
- `src/routes/` — HTTP handlers; thin, delegate to services
- `src/services/` — business logic and orchestration
- `src/db/` or `src/repositories/` — all database access ([sqlx|Diesel])
- `src/error.rs` — the crate's error type (thiserror) and its HTTP mapping
- `tests/` — integration tests against a real database

Layers and their purpose:
- `routes/` → Parse and validate the request, call a service, map errors to responses
- `services/` → Business logic; no SQL here
- `db/` → All database access; one concern per module
- `tests/` → Real-persistence-path tests for P1/P2 (see `rust-patterns.md`)

